{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For therefore I have seen your face.</b> He said to him: take my offering from my hand, because seeing your face is to me like seeing the face of Elohim, and you will be reconciled to me by accepting the offering, just as Elohim desires those who fear Him by accepting their offering and sacrifice — as in <b>\"and it shall be accepted for him\"</b> (Leviticus 1:4), <b>\"Your burnt-offerings and your sacrifices for acceptance upon My altar\"</b> (Isaiah 56:7) — from the language of <b>\"let him be the accepted of his brethren\"</b> (Deuteronomy 33:24), <b>\"and the light of Your face, for You favored them\"</b> (Psalms 44:4), <b>\"for Your servants desired her stones\"</b> (ibid. 102:15) — all of them having the sense of desire and longing for a thing. And Rashi wrote (Rashi on Genesis 33:10): because you reconciled yourself to forgive me for my offenses — <b>\"and you were reconciled to me\"</b> — you were appeased toward me. But I have already said (Ramban on Genesis 32:21) that it is not fitting for him to be reminded of sin."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:38:52.077317013Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}